or_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-06-14T21:06:11Z"},{"id":2928850738,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6ukrcy","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?u=4854f17c9d330a8a9d274f0cb7b943fc2bb6dd44&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","login":"smix8","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107526#pullrequestreview-2928850738","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107526","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-06-14T21:20:14Z"},{"id":2928853119,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6uksB_","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?u=9b90963f1b4f17720e50bbbe495fbe8c84c8bc8e&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","login":"TokageItLab","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107526#pullrequestreview-2928853119","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107526","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-06-14T21:25:03Z"},{"id":3038936049,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc61Invx","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","commit_id":"0a6d67826bc74c89270aa763a8cbea1f2924646f","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?u=9b90963f1b4f17720e50bbbe495fbe8c84c8bc8e&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","login":"TokageItLab","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab"},"body":"I agree with setting the default to empty somewhat. However, since compatibility issues are a concern, so I think at least the following two things are necessary if we make default to emply as break compat in some extent:\r\n\r\n- We need to add a test to verify that the Skeleton Path is assigned correctly during import\r\n- To maintain compatibility with past projects, we will provide a custom node such as SkinMeshInstance3D that automatically searches for the parent skeleton while preserving past behavior. (I guess this could be an add-on or example code rather than being added to the core and can be separate PR from this)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nHowever, if there is no SkeletonPath to begin with, properties such as Skin may not be necessary. Considering that, I think the correct approach would be to divide the classes as mentioned [above](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107526#discussion_r2147339511) into MeshInstance3D and SkinMeshInstance3D, and have SkinMeshInstance3D perform the old MeshInstance3D search behavior (then if SkinMeshInstance3D is not a Skeleton child, a warning should be displayed on SceneTreeDock and can implement use External Skeleton option as I commented in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107526#issuecomment-2973841172). Then MeshInstance3D doesn't need to have `skeleton_path` and `skin` properties to begin with.\r\n\r\nEventually, the problem is that the current MeshInstance3D enforces the intended behavior while being multifunctional only for Skin, even though there are several use cases. Therefore, these classes should be divided according to their roles, and their behavior should be made optional.\r\n\r\nSo I believe the dividing class approach is the most appropriate way. However, a migration manual will be necessary in any case. If the timing is 5.0, I expect that it will be possible to convert classes depending on whether or not `skeleton_path` is used by using the project converter, but if this is done during 4.x, it will be necessary to rely on the manual. (but as long as the scene is imported from an external source, I believe it can be corrected by reimporting)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBased on above, in 4.x, I recommend to implement the three options as enum SkinUsage to MeshInstance3D:\r\n\r\n- `SkinUsage`\r\n  - `SKIN_USAGE_NONE`\r\n  - `SKIN_USAGE_USE_PARENT_SKELETON`\r\n  - `SKIN_USAGE_USE_EXTERNAL_SKELETON`\r\n\r\nYou can make `SKIN_USAGE_NONE` default, at this point, if the .tscn have skeleton_path, you should be able to set `SKIN_USAGE_USE_EXTERNAL_SKELETON` in the `#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED` block in the setter. And at last, provide a manual that sets `SKIN_USAGE_USE_PARENT_SKELETON` only for those who have projects that depend on search operations.\r\n\r\nand, at the time of the 5.0 launch, replace the `SKIN_USAGE_NONE` option with a MeshInstance3D that does not have a skin, and split the `SKIN_USAGE_USE_PARENT_SKELETON` and `SKIN_USAGE_USE_EXTERNAL_SKELETON` options into an extended class called SkinMeshInstance3D. I believe this is a reasonable compromise for minimizing compatibility breaks.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107526#pullrequestreview-3038936049","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107526","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-07-21T16:53:09Z"}]